AIHack modifications
--------------------

AIHack contributors rewrote and modified the derivative work during 2025 and
2026. The rewrite replaces the original implementation architecture with a
Rust workspace, deterministic state transactions, embedded content, replay,
headless and TUI adapters, and guarded LLM assistance.

Modification record: all project-owned files under `src/`, `crates/`, `apps/`,
`tests/`, `scripts/`, and `docs/`, together with the root build and project
documents, were created or changed for the AIHack rewrite during 2025-2026.
The distributed `MODIFICATIONS.md` carries the path scopes, change period and
modification descriptions. `RELEASE-METADATA` identifies the exact source
commit covered by that manifest. These records do not depend on a distributed
`.git/` directory. More specific provenance records are maintained in
`PROVENANCE.md`.

No claim is made that AIHack is an official NetHack release or is endorsed by
the NetHack copyright holders. Original NetHack notices present in retained
reference material remain intact.

Distribution and source availability
------------------------------------

AIHack is distributed under the NGPL terms in LICENSE. Every AIHack binary
release must be accompanied by LICENSE, this NOTICE, MODIFICATIONS.md,
PROJECT_OWNER_LICENSE_APPROVAL.md, RELEASE-METADATA, SHA256SUMS, and the
complete corresponding source used to build that release. The approval and
modification IDs in RELEASE-METADATA must each occur exactly once and resolve
by complete-value equality to the IDs in those bundled records. The build scripts create an
`aihack-0.3.0-source` archive from the release commit for this purpose.

The `legacy_nethack_port_reference/` tree is retained only as historical
reference and is excluded from AIHack release archives. Its local damaged
license copy is not used as the operative license for AIHack releases.
